estserver: no mock CA; the TACRA backend alone, and a strict configuration

The group's server creates a mock CA at every start (a transient one when the configuration names none), issues its own
TLS certificate from it when the configuration has no tls section, and uses it as the CA behind the EST resources unless
a tacra section replaces it. This bench's server runs only with the TACRA backend: the mock CA, the mock attested CA
(attest) and the self-issued server certificate are out, and the tls and tacra sections are required. With tacra always
present, TLS 1.3 is always the minimum.

The configuration is decoded strictly, as the group's is: mock_ca, attest, any field the server does not know, or data
after the object is an error. The sample (-sampleconfig) is in the TACRA backend's shape, as estserver.json.example
already is. config_test.go checks that both parse, and that the mock CA's sections, a missing section, a missing key
file and a misspelt field are refused.

internal/mockca stays for the upstream tests that use it; the server no longer imports it. The bench's rule, not the
group's: patch 0009 of the series the bench carried until 11 October 2026, on the group's master since then.

